module gunbc.plans.derived_types_keep_their_name

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.markdown_helpers { h2, p, quote, li, ul }

// Planning-only intention. It organises rulings that already exist; it adds no ruling. A decision it
// needs from the operator -- whether the bare-alias declaration form leaves the language -- is raised
// for a ruling (gunbc.design_ruling) and cited, never asserted here.
// It is the answer to the operator's 2026-11-19 question "I thought we were getting rid of aliases?":
// the where-refinement retirement IS ruled, a blanket "no aliases" is NOT, and the measured reason a
// refined/branded/aliased type is interchangeable with its base is the checker's own alias/refinement
// transparency, not a missing argument check.

fn derived_types_keep_their_name_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    quote(blocks: [
      p(text: "**This plan is written as an intention** (`gunbc.design_argument::plans_are_intentions`): it holds what, why and done-when, never the how. Work items, their order and their staffing are selected against this intention and live under the roadmap in `gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_authority`; a work item names this intention, the intention does not list its work items."),
      p(text: "**Grounding (existing rulings, cited not minted):** `gunbc.design_ruling::where_refinements_retire_for_checked_constructors` (where-refinements leave the language, replaced by checked constructors returning Optional), `gunbc.design_ruling::nonemptiness_is_constructed_or_proved`, `gunbc.design_ruling::machine_width_composition_has_an_intersection_carrier` (Compose is an intersection carrier, not a transparent alias), `gunbc.design_ruling::literal_only_refinement_judgment_is_interim` (the interim literal admission the eventual v2 cut retires). **Motivating arguments:** `gunbc.design_argument::single_authority` (a second name for one concept is nicknaming), `gunbc.design_argument::replacement_migration`, `gunbc.design_argument::root_generalization` (whose failure example (a) is literally Type-alias identity), `gunbc.design_argument::closed_grounded_substrate`."),
      p(text: "**Honest scope:** there is NO blanket ruling that bans type aliases. Ruled: the retirement of `where`-refinements. Not ruled: removing the bare-alias declaration form from the language -- nickname aliases are discouraged by `single_authority` but deleting the form is an operator decision raised for a ruling, not inferred here. This intention commits only to refusing the *interchangeability* -- a base value standing in for its derived type at a check the compiler judges."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "1. Intention (what)"),
    p(text: "**What:** a type that a declaration derives from another type by refinement, brand, or a bare name is not interchangeable with its base at a judgment the compiler makes. Passing a value whose type is the base into a position whose declared type is the derived type, or the reverse, is decided by ONE inhabitance rule that has the symbol table in hand; it is never waved through because the two names settle to a common head. `where`-refinements are reached only through a checked constructor returning Optional or through carried evidence (cited: `where_refinements_retire_for_checked_constructors`, `nonemptiness_is_constructed_or_proved`). What is NOT touched: an abbreviation of a parameterized type, and the Compose/phantom intersection forms governed by `machine_width_composition_has_an_intersection_carrier` -- those claim no guarantee and stay admitted."),
    p(text: "**Why (operator, 2026-11-19):** the operator believed aliases were being removed. They are, but only in the ruled slice (the `where`-refinements), and nothing on the required path currently refuses a plain String reaching a `NonEmptyStr`, branded, or even `nominal_opaque` parameter. The guarantee the operators think they have -- that a name like `PathSegment` or `CommitSha` means something the checker enforces -- is not on the path that judges code."),
    h2(text: "2. Why -- the measured hole, and the rulings this realizes"),
    p(text: "On the v1 seed CompileAccept path -- the path the required gate and `gunbc run --claim-run` use -- a probe suite (scratch module `probe.alias_interchange`, harness `gunbc.compile_diagnostic_census`, one process, never committed; recorded in `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode::an_int_argument_inhabits_a_nat_parameter_at_typecheck`) shows the general call-argument-vs-parameter check FIRES: an `Int` at a declared record parameter, a `String` variable at a declared record parameter, and an `Int` at a declared `String` parameter are each refused with a blocking row, and the base-at-base and derived-at-derived controls are clean. Yet every SAME-BASE derived type is silently accepted with ZERO blocking rows of any class: a `String` variable at a `std.types` `NonEmptyStr` parameter (`where string_non_empty`), at a branded `std.types` `PathSegment` (`NonEmptyStr where brand(\"PathSegment\")`), at a local bare nickname `type MyStr = String`, and at a local `type MySecret nominal_opaque = String`. The arguments are String-typed VARIABLES, never literals, so the interim literal admission (`literal_only_refinement_judgment_is_interim`) is not the admitting cause; a `NonEmptyStr`-at-`NonEmptyStr` control is clean, so the names resolve and these are admitted arguments, not unresolved ones."),
    p(text: "So the hole is the alias/refinement transparency inside `v1.compiler.infer` `declared_type_inhabitance`: a bare alias is collapsed by `v1.compiler.infer_env` `alias_identity_in_judgment` to Inhabits, and a base at a `where`-refinement is `refinement_inhabitance` returning Undecidable (`UndecidableRefinementIntroduction`), which the application does not treat as blocking -- so even `nominal_opaque` does not refuse its base at argument position on this path. This is exactly `root_generalization` failure example (a): alias identity decided by per-call-site fallbacks instead of one rule with the symbol table. The realization is the ONE root inhabitance rule; the ordered steps, their sizes, and the migration surfaces are work-item selections against this intention, not part of it."),
    h2(text: "3. Done-when"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "The four probe cases each refuse on the required path with a blocking row, and their discriminating RED (the suite above) turns green: a base value at a where-refinement, a brand, a bare nickname, and a `nominal_opaque` parameter are each refused, while base-at-base and derived-at-derived stay clean -- decided once by the root inhabitance rule, not by a per-call-site fallback."),
      li(text: "Every `where`-refinement is reached only through a checked constructor returning Optional or carried evidence (the condition of `where_refinements_retire_for_checked_constructors`), and the literal-only interim admission is retired in favour of expected-type literal introduction."),
      li(text: "Legitimate abbreviations of a parameterized type and the Compose/phantom intersection forms REMAIN admitted (refusing them would collide with `machine_width_composition_has_an_intersection_carrier`)."),
      li(text: "An ordering constraint (reasoning, not a phase list): retiring nickname aliases is not complete while base-to-derived interchange is still admitted -- a site quietly relying on the collapse must not be broken by removing the name before the interchange is refused."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "4. Realization (downstream)"),
    p(text: "The ordered steps, their sizes, their seed-versus-v2 boundaries under `gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing::v1_seed_standing`, and the migration surfaces are realized as work items under the roadmap in `gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_authority`, each bound to this intention via `gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_intention_binding` and each carrying its own red control and first slice, so a landing is read against the guarantee it serves -- which derived type moved from interchangeable to refused at the argument, which `where`-refinement lost its predicate to a checked constructor -- never a count of files rewritten."),
  ]
}

data derived_types_keep_their_name_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly,
  slug: "derived-types-keep-their-name",
  title: "Derived types keep their name: a refined, branded or nickname type stops standing in for its base at an argument, and where-refinements retire to checked constructors",
  body: derived_types_keep_their_name_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Section 3 is achieved: no base value stands in for a derived type at an argument position on the required path (the four-case discriminating RED green, decided by one root inhabitance rule), and every where-refinement is reached by a checked constructor or carried evidence, with the legitimate abbreviation and intersection forms still admitted.") },
}
